  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale\nThe current approach achieves a bound of 0.380920 and we aim to improve upon it by 0.00012. While the local optimization in the provided code identifies promising regions, it may get stuck in local optima. We will enhance exploration through a two-stage hybrid search: (a) adaptive multi-resolution construction that transfers structure from the parent solution to higher resolutions, and (b) gradient-based local refinement using differentiable reformulations. This combines structure transfer from the parent with local optimization to escape known local optima.\n\n2. Mathematical specification\n- Representation: h(x)\u2208[0,1] with \u222bh(x)dx=1, sampled at n_points\u2208\u211d\n- Objective: minimize max_k \u222bh(x)(1-h(x+k))dx\n- Transformation to equivalent problem: \n  Let y(x)=h(x)-0.5, then \u222by(x)dx=0 and y(x)\u2208[-0.5,0.5]\n  Define F(y)=\u222b [1 - sign(1/(1+exp(-4*y))-0.5] (Note: difference in \u2265(y) vs \u2264(y))\n- Discretization: \n  Sum = \u2211y_i * \u0394x \u2248 0 (with \u0394x=2/n_points)\n  Scaled correlations: \u2200k, max_k [\u2211_{i} y_i * [y_{i+k} + 0.5] * \u0394x^2 ] (from discrete differentiability)\n\n3. Implementation procedure\n- Parent validation:\n  - Verify n_points=70, initial_h_values has values in [0,1]\n  - Compute strict integral: if abs(\u222bh(x)dx-1)>1e-8 return fallback\n- Initialization:\n  Stage1: Active lag optimization with adaptive penalty (\u03b2=100, top_k=10)\n  - Initialize from h_parent and h_uniform\n  - Phase1: smooth_max (\u03b2=100) with gradient descent (over lags)\n- Multi-resolution strategy:\n  Stage2: Resolution expansion from 70 to 110:\n  - Maintain parent-induced structure: create transition matrix from 70 to 110 points\n  - Select K_best=3 offspring from uniform and structured approaches\n- Local refinement:\n  - Four-phase optimization with:\n    Phase4: Bayesian optimization (50 steps) with Gaussian process surrogate\n    Phase5: Differential evolution for worst offenders\n  - Constraint handling: Projection via least-squares with integral constraint\n\n4. Search choices\n- Resolution sweep: [70, 90, 110, 130] (prioritize 70->110 path)\n- Stochastic elements:\n  - Initial sampling: Sobol sequence (avoid random starts)\n  - Lag selection: Top K using next-to-max correlations\n- Tangential variations:\n  - Replace gradient descent with ADAM for faster convergence\n  - Lag-based vs point-based optimization (with switch to structured)\n\n5. Budget allocation\n- Warm-up: 60s for 70-point refinement (starting from parent)\n- Main: 800s for resolution expansion (70->110->130)\n- Exploration: 200s for Bayesian optimization\n- Fallback: 40s for DE polishing\n- Key timings:\n  - Resolution sweep: 40s per resolution point\n  - Bayesian phase: 20s for 50 steps\n  - Projection: limited to O(10) iterations\n\n6. Validation\n- Integral check: abs(\u2211y_i * \u0394x) < 1e-5\n- Bounds: [-0.5,0.5] scaled from parent\n- Final output:\n  - Best=70: fallback to parent if needed\n  - Best=110/130: validate against known constraints\n- Graceful degradation:\n  - If phase times expire, save best valid solution\n  - If projection fails, return best post-parent optimization",
